  "Source": "A. Vasicek, \"Multiple thin dielectric films as mirrors and interference filters,\" Czech. J. Phys. 3, 206-222 (1953). doi:10.1007/BF01687127 - Sec. II, p. 208 (indices, Fig. 1b, odd k with H first and last); Eqs. (35)-(37) p. 212; Tables I and III (pp. 213, 215), Table IV upper part (p. 222)",
  "Notes": "Quarter-wave high/low dielectric mirror on glass with k = 3 films (odd, H outermost and next to the glass), light incident from air\nSpecification: Maximum reflectance at 550 nm (path difference x = 180 deg in every film, i.e. quarter waves): air | H L H | glass\nReported: Normal incidence from air, rear glass surface ignored. Table I (p. 213): R = 71.227 %, T = 1-R = 28.773 % at x = 180 deg (550 nm); equivalent single quarter-wave index N = 4.2353 (Eq. 37, N^2 = n1^(k+1)/n2^(k-1)). Table III (p. 215), exact R % vs path difference x (x = 180 deg at 550 nm, so x corresponds to wavelength 550*180/x nm, non-dispersive indices): x=10 deg (9900 nm) 5.5104; x=30 deg (3300 nm) 12.162; x=60 deg (1650 nm) 12.538; x=90 deg (1100 nm) 2.9332; x=105 deg (942.9 nm) 13.856; x=120 deg (825 nm) 34.715; x=135 deg (733.3 nm) 52.709; x=150 deg (660 nm) 63.853; x=180 deg (550 nm) 71.227.\nNotes: Path difference x = (2 pi/lambda) 2 n d (Eq. 2), so x = 180 deg is a quarter wave; all films have the same x (Eq. 12). Indices are wavelength independent (n1 = 2.40, n2 = 1.36, glass BK7 n = 1.518 at 550 nm), so Table III columns at other x equal this quarter-wave-at-550-nm stack evaluated at lambda = 550*180/x nm (the paper itself maps x to wavelength this way in Figs. 5 and 9). Absorption neglected; single coated surface, no back-surface reflection. Stack is symmetric so listing order is the same from either side.\nLayers from Sec. II, p. 208 (indices, Fig. 1b, odd k with H first and last); Eqs. (35)-(37) p. 212; Tables I and III (pp. 213, 215), Table IV upper part (p. 222); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 0.712257 at 550 nm; paper R 0.7122700000000001 (printed).",
